{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795771299,"nonce":"Bq4iP73v5rMXt7Ax4d4uja46eQQ=","title":"corner-shape: round in CSS is replaced by the theme's corner smoothing","message":"resolve_corner_shape treats a round shape as unset, so an explicit corner-shape: round, or .corner_shape(round), draws the theme's squircle on corners over the smoothing threshold. Any other shape is kept. Seen writing a shadow pixel test under BlincTheme: a 20px corner with corner-shape: round drew a superellipse. The theme should yield to a shape that was set, which the property tiers can tell.","files":null}]}